    "intro_html":  "Pastel de choclo is Chile\u0027s answer to shepherd\u0027s pie, except the topping is sweet corn instead of mashed potato and it is scented with fresh basil. Underneath sits pino, the seasoned beef and onion filling studded with olives, raisins, and hard boiled egg. Chileans argue about the raisins the way Americans argue about beans in chili, so put them in and take a side. The corn layer bakes into something between a custard and a cornbread, and the whole tray cuts into squares.",
